```
labels: paths[1][2] | paths[2][1] | paths[2][2]
answer: 1 | 1 | 2
wrong[2 | 2 | 4]: The rock at (1, 1) has 0 paths, so it adds nothing to the cells to its right and below it.
wrong[1 | 1 | 6]: Without the rock, there would be 6 paths. With it, only the two around the edges remain.
wrong[1 | 1 | 1]: (2, 2) adds the cell above, 1, and the cell to its left, 1: 2.
