* Both last characters can't end the same common subsequence, so one of them can be dropped: the box above drops a's, the box to the left drops b's, and the better choice wins :: Right. The LCS of the shorter pair is already known.
- Because the diagonal box is always smaller :: The point is which characters can be left out, not the sizes of the boxes.
- Because a mismatch ends the subsequence :: A subsequence can skip characters; a mismatch only means one of the two isn't used here.
